                <pb facs="0144" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg102"/>


                <head>American Minister, London, to Mr. Sprague, American Consul, Gibraltar.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 19, 1863—12.30 <hi rendition="#italic">p.
                            m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Sumter should be captured if she goes out of the British waters on the high
                    seas. If she have nominal British papers she must be sent home for adjudication
                    as prize.</p>
                <p>Please notify the naval commanders.</p>
            </div>
